From 870b20d6efd61778204eab7e1e4c140e0c14b8d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:58:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: offload ChronikValidationInterface callbacks to
 dedicated worker thread

Add a dedicated background worker thread and bounded FIFO task queue to ChronikValidationInterface so Chronik indexing events execute in strict FIFO order off the shared ValidationSignals scheduler thread.

Original-Commit: fcea86012096e7f339ec3ed4f3d6790cb628334b
Original-Patch: ecash/049
Split-Concern: whole

Folded owner repair: both validation synchronization entrypoints also fence the
secondary FIFO. The worker bypasses its own fence; shutdown drain belongs to
StopWorker/join. Native regressions prove both entrypoints wait for indexing.
Full Chronik-enabled prefix validation remains required at this boundary.

Plan-v2 owner repair: C: bound secondary Chronik work and retained payload memory, fail closed on overload/allocation/worker exceptions, and drain accepted work with an ordered fence. Final worker and memory helpers match the recorded400-transaction diagnostic exactly.

